    <p class="rtecenter">On February 5, the Georgetown DMV Service Center experienced a significant water main break. Due to flooding impacts, the Georgetown DMV Service Center will remain closed to the public until further notice.&nbsp;DC DMV's services will remain available at our&nbsp;<a href="https://dmv.dc.gov/page/all-dc-dmv-locations" data-auth="NotApplicable" data-linkindex="4" data-ogsc="blue" rel="noreferrer noopener" title="https://dmv.dc.gov/page/all-dc-dmv-locations"><u>other locations</u></a>, <a href="https://dmv.dc.gov/service/dmv-online-services" aria-label="Link online" id="menurcae" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" title="https://dmv.dc.gov/service/dmv-online-services">online</a> and via our <a href="https://dmv.dc.gov/service/dc-dmv-mobile-app" aria-label="Link free mobile app" id="menurcag" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" title="https://dmv.dc.gov/service/dc-dmv-mobile-app">mobile app</a>.</p><p class="rtecenter">&nbsp;</p><p class="rtecenter">Due to a systemic issue with real-time authorization,&nbsp;the&nbsp;ACH/Electronic Check payment feature has&nbsp;been&nbsp;temporarily&nbsp;removed from all DMV online and mobile app transactions. Our team is working with the Office of the Chief Financial Officer (OCFO) to resolve the matter.&nbsp;Contactless, credit/debit card, cash, and check payments continue to be accepted in person.</p>
